---

## Test Smell Audit — `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 · **.NET 10** · **Integration test class** (`[TestCategory("Integration")]`)

Integration calibration applied: Mystery Guest / Eager Test / Sleepy Test severity adjusted per integration-test norms.

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High | 3 | 3 |
| Medium | 1 | 1 |
| Total | **4** | **4** |

**Clean tests (4/8):** `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted`, `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` — well-structured, focused, and properly asserted.

---

### Findings by Severity

---

#### ❶ Conditional Test Logic — HIGH

**Smell:** Control flow (`if`/`else`) changes which assertion runs, so one branch is never exercised.

**Location:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);   // ← only runs if PremiumUser
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);       // ← only runs otherwise
}
```

**Risk:** One branch is dead code for a given run — hidden testing gap. If the return type changes, the test silently switches branches instead of failing.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

#### ❷ Sleepy Test — HIGH

**Smell:** `Thread.Sleep` introduces a hard 3-second wall-clock wait. Even in integration tests this remains a smell — it slows the suite and is non-deterministic (the delay may be too short on a loaded CI agent or needlessly long otherwise).

**Location:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // ← blocks thread for 3 s
```

**Risk:** Flaky under load; suite gets slower as more such tests accumulate.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    // Poll up to 5 s, checking every 100 ms
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow.AddSeconds(5);
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
            break;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }

    Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        "Notification was not sent within the expected timeout.");
}
```

---

#### ❸ Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test) — HIGH

**Smell:** The test executes 100 inserts but never asserts anything. MSTest reports it as "passed" even if every insert silently corrupts data.

**Location:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← no assertions
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate with zero verification.

**Fix — assert the observable outcome:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count,
        "All 100 bulk-inserted users should be retrievable.");
}
```

---

#### ❹ Assertion Roulette — MEDIUM

**Smell:** 4 assertions with no failure messages. When one fails, the CI log shows a bare `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no indication of *which* property was wrong.

**Location:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Risk:** Increased triage time — developers must open the source to understand failures.

**Fix — add failure messages:**

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should be persisted.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should be persisted.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Inserted user should receive a positive ID.");
```

---

### Smells Not Found (15/19 clean)

| Smell | Status |
|-------|--------|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ In-memory SQLite — hermetic, no external dependency |
| Eager Test | ✅ No test calls 4+ distinct production methods |
| Magic Number Test | ✅ Counts (3, 10, 100) are self-documenting in context |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ No `ToString()`-based comparisons |
| Exception Handling | ✅ No `try`/`catch` in tests |
| General Fixture | ✅ `_connection` and `_repository` used by every test |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ No skipped tests |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ No identical assertions |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Shared method calls serve distinct behavioral scenarios |
| Constructor Init | ✅ Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly |
| Default Test | ✅ Meaningful class name |
| Redundant Print | ✅ No debug output |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ No tautological assertions |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ No assumed-present external resources |
| Empty Test | ✅ No empty methods |

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Why first |
|----------|-------|--------|-----------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** (`BulkInsert`) | ~2 min | Currently a false-pass — zero verification |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** (`GetUser`) | ~10 min | Hidden gap — one branch never tested |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** (`NotifyOnInsert`) | ~10 min | 3 s wall-clock drag + flake risk |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** (`InsertUser`) | ~2 min | Quick win — add message strings |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean and well-structured. The 4 findings are real but tractable — roughly 25 minutes of work to resolve all of them.
